## Enchace idea

Currently launch() and launchContext() both use browser.launch() + browser.newContext(), which always creates incognito/ephemeral contexts. This is detected by multiple anti-bot services:

- BrowserScan flags it as "Incognito mode: Yes" with a -10% penalty
- FingerprintJS can distinguish incognito from normal sessions via storage API behavior
- CreepJS checks FileSystem API availability which differs in incognito

This undermines the stealth that CloakBrowser's 26 C++ patches provide. A browser can have perfect canvas, WebGL, audio, and font fingerprints — but if it's detected as incognito, it's immediately suspicious. Real users rarely browse in incognito, especially when creating accounts or making purchases.

The root cause: Playwright's browser.newContext() creates isolated BrowserContexts that behave identically to incognito mode — no persistent storage, no cookies from previous sessions, limited FileSystem API access. The only way to get a non-incognito context in Playwright is chromium.launchPersistentContext() with a userDataDir.

## Current workaround

Since CloakBrowser doesn't export a persistent context launcher, we import internal modules directly and wire them into Playwright's native chromium.launchPersistentContext(). Full working example (JS):

    import { chromium } from 'playwright-core';
    import path from 'path';
    import { fileURLToPath } from 'url';

    const { resolveProxyGeo } = await import('file:///path/to/node_modules/cloakbrowser/dist/geoip.js');
    const { parseProxyUrl } = await import('file:///path/to/node_modules/cloakbrowser/dist/proxy.js');
    const { getDefaultStealthArgs } = await import('file:///path/to/node_modules/cloakbrowser/dist/config.js');

    const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
    const profileDir = path.join(__dirname, 'chrome-profile');
    const binary = binaryInfo().binaryPath;
    const proxyStr = 'http://user:pass@host:port';

    const { timezone, locale } = await resolveProxyGeo(proxyStr);
    const stealthArgs = getDefaultStealthArgs();
    const proxyParsed = parseProxyUrl(proxyStr);

    const context = await chromium.launchPersistentContext(profileDir, {
      executablePath: binary,
      headless: false,
      viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 },
      timezoneId: timezone,
      locale: locale,
      ignoreDefaultArgs: ['--enable-automation'],
      args: stealthArgs,
      proxy: proxyParsed,
    });

    const page = context.pages()[0] || await context.newPage();
    await page.goto('https://browserscan.net/');
    // BrowserScan now shows: Incognito mode: No

This works, but has problems: relies on internal module paths (dist/geoip.js, dist/config.js, dist/proxy.js) not part of the public API; requires file:// URL imports because the modules are ESM but not listed in package.json exports; users must manually find the binary path; could break on any update; not documented.

## Proposed API

A new exported function wrapping Playwright's chromium.launchPersistentContext() with the same stealth defaults, geoip resolution, and proxy handling that launch() already provides.

JavaScript:

    import { launchPersistentContext } from 'cloakbrowser';

    const context = await launchPersistentContext({
      userDataDir: './chrome-profile',
      headless: false,
      proxy: 'http://user:pass@host:port',
      geoip: true,
      viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 },
    });

    const page = context.pages()[0] || await context.newPage();
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
    await context.close();

Python:

    from cloakbrowser import launch_persistent_context

    context = launch_persistent_context(
        user_data_dir="./chrome-profile",
        headless=False,
        proxy="http://user:pass@host:port",
        geoip=True,
    )

    page = context.pages[0] if context.pages else context.new_page()
    page.goto("https://example.com")
    context.close()

The function should: auto-download/locate the stealth binary, apply default stealth args, support geoip: true for auto timezone/locale, parse proxy URL strings, set ignoreDefaultArgs: ['--enable-automation'], and accept all standard Playwright launchPersistentContext options as passthrough.

